  "goodToKnow": "Die Heuschrecke is a grasshopper or locust; swarms of Wanderheuschrecken are a biblical plague. In 2005, SPD chairman Franz Müntefering compared certain private equity investors to Heuschrecken that descend on companies, strip them and move on, sparking the Heuschreckendebatte about capitalism. The name comes from Heu (hay) and an old verb schrecken meaning to jump. Plural: die Heuschrecken."
